"""The Sunward Crown's story pass (22 Nov 2026), to docs/quest_writing_standard.md, written after Lenswatch took in the
Annex and the survey's two scholars and Spearhold became the trolls' own small camp map (Kyle: "Tiny camp, no hearth or
flight. But seperate map"). Every speech is the giver talking from where they now stand; every accept line is a new
beat."""

STORY = {
    'scq_every_spear': (
        "I sit by de broken mural and tie a knot in dis cord for every climber who comes up through de wall. De war-leader wants to know how many spears he's got, and he wants every one of dem who can fight. Spearhold is west of here, at de back of de crown, where de trolls camp. I've tied two hundred knots since de seal cracked, mon. Take him de tally, and take yourself wit' it.",
        "Rakkuzi counts de knots twice. Don't let him see you laugh when he does."),
    'scq_spears_on_the_crown': (
        "De sky people walked onto our tree and called it a meetin', and den their soldiers fell on de meetin'. Every Ascendancy Legionary on de north arm, north-east of Spearhold, stands in one line wit' his shield locked, like de tree is a wall dey're guardin'. Zan'kaji sent me up here to throw dem off it. Go up de arm and break dat line. I want dem to know de Highbough don't ask politely.",
        "Hit de line where de shields meet. Dat's where it bends."),
    'scq_centurion_valeth_krane': (
        "Your envoy proved de scholars didn't call de soldiers down, and fine, I believe him. Dey're still on my tree. Centurion Valeth Krane holds de north arm, north-east of Spearhold, and while he stands, his line stands. I lost nine spears to dat line. Go up dere and put him down.",
        'Bring me his helmet. De Highbough will want to see it on a pole.'),
    'scq_count_the_lancers': (
        "I've counted de Ascendancy's lancers twice from dis branch, and both times I came back wit' a bigger number. I can't get past de humming poles wit'out dem seein' me, but you might. Their fort is on de Taken Crown, up de north arm, north-east of Spearhold. Get a proper look inside it. Count de tents and count de guns.",
        "Don't stop to fight anyting dat don't stop you first. You're a scout today."),
    'scq_humming_poles': (
        "De poles on de Taken Crown hum because of de Ascendancy Shield Drones floatin' round dem. Every drone carries a lens of blue crystal, and I tink dat's what holds de shield up. De fort is up de north arm, north-east of here. I watched one drone fall last week, and de shield on dat side flickered. Bring me dose Shield Foci, and I'll find out how to make dem all stop.",
        'De drones drift in a circle. Wait for one to come round to you.'),
    'scq_rays_over_the_islets': (
        "My wyverns won't go near de Driftlets, de islets chained off de south side of de cloud, south-east of Spearhold. De Drift Rays glide round dem like dey own de sky, and every Cloud Jelly stings anyting dat comes close. My wyverns never shook in their lives before dey came up here. Now dey shake every night. Thin dem out, and maybe my wyverns will remember dey're wyverns.",
        "De jellies drift wit' de wind. Stand upwind and dey come to you slow."),
    'scq_mother_greatfin': (
        "Dere's a whale out over de Driftlets de size of a longhouse, and de others follow her like calves. I call her Mother Greatfin. My wyverns won't leave their roosts while she's singin', and she sings all day. De Driftlets are south-east of Spearhold, out over de chains. Go out and bring her down.",
        "When she sings, she stops movin'. Dat's your moment."),
    'scq_eels_at_the_falls': (
        "My wyverns drink at de Falls of Light, south of Spearhold, and de Falls Eels have already taken two of dem off de bank. De Mossback Tortoises are worse, because dey'll sit in de water and wait like a rock. I raised one of dose wyverns from an egg, mon. De bank is on de south side of de crown, where de spring runs over. Clear de bank, so de rest of dem can drink.",
        "Poke every rock in de shallows wit' your spear. Some of dem bite back."),
    'scq_old_sunantler': (
        "Up in de Goldenwood on de north arm, north of Spearhold, dere's a stag de others won't walk in front of. His antlers catch de sun and throw it back at you, and de trolls who've seen him call him Old Sunantler. No rider on de crown has earned a trophy yet. Every one of us wants him. I want you to get him first.",
        "Come at him wit' de sun behind you, or his antlers will blind you."),
    'scq_spirits_in_the_light': (
        "Dere's a ring of old stone out on de cloud, east of Spearhold and north-east of de stones where de parley was. Light is leakin' up out of de middle of it, and Seal-Touched Shades are comin' up wit' de light. Dey're not spirits I know, and de loa go quiet when I ask about dem. Dat's never happened to me before. Send dem back where dey came from.",
        "Burn a bit of sage before you go. It won't help, but it'll make me feel better."),
    'scq_what_the_loa_wont_say': (
        "If de loa won't tell me what dat ring is, den I'll ask somebody who can read it, and dat hurts my pride. De Waking Guardians round de ring are cut all over wit' old runes. Bring de Rune-Cut Shards off dem to de pale archivist who used to sit by de ring. He's moved into Lenswatch, over de gangway on de east edge of de cloud. Tell him a troll witch doctor sent you.",
        "I'd like to see his face when you tell him. Remember it for me."),
    'scq_two_brothers': (
        "My brothers went past de humming poles before any of us knew what de lancers could do. De Ascendancy Sky Lancers on de Taken Crown took their spears and carry dem like prizes. I can see dem from here, mon, swingin' my brothers' spears like dey earned dem. Bring dem back to me. I want to give dem to our mother, because she'll never get anyting else.",
        "My brothers carved snakes into de shafts. You'll know dem."),
    'scq_the_dewdrinker': (
        "Dere's an eel in de Falls of Light as long as a canoe, and it drinks from de spring like it's been doin' it for a hundred years. I call it de Dewdrinker. I've had my spear in it twice, and twice it pulled me under. My ribs are still tellin' me about de second time. Go and finish what I started.",
        'It comes up to breathe every time de light shifts on de water. Watch de light.'),
    'scq_both_sides_of_the_stones': (
        "The Warchief sent me to keep the Horde out of a war it doesn't understand. The war-leader says the scholars called their soldiers down on the parley, and the scholars say they didn't. Only one troll was standing on those stones when it happened, and that's Speaker Hezza. The Parley Stones are east of Spearhold, out on the cloud. Take her my token so she knows I sent you, and hear what she has to say.",
        "Don't bring Rakkuzi. Hezza won't say a true word with him glaring at her."),
    'scq_carry_it_to_the_war_leader': (
        "The scholar didn't call his soldiers down, and here's the proof in his own writing. Rakkuzi won't take it from me, because I'm Orgrimmar's and he thinks I want to stop his war. I do, but that's not why it's true. He might take it from you, because you've bled on that arm. Take it to him at the fire.",
        "Hand it to him, don't read it to him. He'll want to hold the proof."),
    'scq_what_hezza_saw': (
        "Look at de ship dat came down on us, de burnt one at de edge of de stones. De marks on its side are de soldiers' marks, not de scholars'. I stood right here when it fell, and I saw de scholars run from it same as us. When you've seen de marks, go and tell Ilaren Vey, de pale one who stood across from me. He's in Lenswatch now, over de gangway east of here.",
        "He'll read de marks better dan either of us. Tell him Hezza sent you."),
    'scq_orders_under_seal': (
        "Every Ascendancy Legionary carries his orders sealed in crystal, so he can't forget them and can't change them. The legionaries on the Taken Crown, west of Lenswatch up the north arm, will be carrying the orders for the parley. They're my own people, and they fired on me without a word. Bring me their Sealed Legion Orders. I'll show your envoy what my own people meant to do.",
        "Don't crack the crystal. If it's whole, nobody can say I wrote the orders myself."),
    'scq_the_light_under_the_stones': (
        "Krane's dead and the stone's down, and the light under the seal is brighter than it's ever been. I've asked Rakkuzi, your envoy and Elyon to meet me at the old ring, and to everyone's surprise they've all said yes. The ring is out on the cloud, west of Lenswatch. Whatever happens next, someone from every side should see it. Come and stand with us.",
        "Stand between Rakkuzi and Elyon. They'll both behave if you're in the middle."),
    'scq_bigger_than_the_ascendancy': (
        "My house has argued for a hundred years about whether the ground is worth talking to. We were arguing about the wrong thing. I've written down everything that happened at the seal, every word, and it isn't the report I expected to write. Take this to the surveyor in the court. Tell him I said to send it to the council tonight, not tomorrow.",
        "The Ascendancy isn't the worst thing in the sky any more. Tell him I said that too."),
    'scq_a_guest_of_the_house': (
        "I keep the gangway to Lenswatch, the survey's town, and the surveyor has asked to meet every climber who comes up through the wall. You're the one I've got today. Lenswatch is just across the gangway, on its island off the east edge of the cloud. Take this pass over and give it to Surveyor-Captain Destren in the court. They'll give you a bed there, which is more than the trolls will.",
        'Hold the rail on the gangway. The wind off the cloud likes to take newcomers.'),
    'scq_what_the_ground_thinks': (
        "Your herbalists call it sungrass, and it does something no plant in the upper sky can do. It holds the day's light and gives it back at dusk. I've watched it glow from the court every evening since we anchored here. It grows all over the crown, west of Lenswatch across the gangway. Gather me some, because I'd like to know why the tree can make something my whole people can't.",
        "Pick it at dusk if you can. That's when it's holding the most light."),
    'scq_lance_captain_varos_thale': (
        "The council has answered, and it's the answer I hoped for. Aurelion will open its gates to the ground for the first time in our history, and they're sending their own skiff down to the crown. Lance-Captain Varos Thale holds the Chainhold, the islet chained off the north edge of the cloud, north-west of Lenswatch. He'll shoot the council's skiff out of the sky. Cross the chains and put him down.",
        "When he falls, look up. The council's skiff will already be on its way."),
    'scq_the_stolen_copy': (
        "I write everything down twice, and when the soldiers came down on the stones they took my first copy of everything we'd learned. It's on the Chainhold now, the islet chained off the north edge of the cloud, north-west of Lenswatch. The Ascendancy Bombardiers and Artillerists there carry the pages folded up in their packs and pass them round. My second copy is good, but the first one has the drawings. Bring me my Stolen Survey Pages, every one you can find.",
        "If they've drawn in the margins, I still want the page. I'll draw round it."),
    'scq_mark_the_rifts': (
        "The great lens looks straight through cloud, and that's the trouble, because it can't tell me where the cloud stops holding you up. There are three tears in the shelf west of Lenswatch I want marked. One is north-west of the Survey Dock, one is south-east of the Parley Stones, and one is south of the dock. I lost a porter through one of them last month, and I'd like it to be the last. Stand at the edge of each one so I can fix it in the lens.",
        "Don't stand too close to the edge. I'd hate to fix you in the lens on your way down."),
    'scq_storm_readings': (
        "The Stormbank, the dark cloud south-west of Lenswatch, has been getting darker every day, and the lens can't see into it at all. The Bolt-Born Elementals in it leave Charged Motes when they come apart, and each mote holds a little of the storm's charge. Bring me some so I can read how much it's holding. I've never seen a cloud hold that much charge without breaking. While you're in there, keep the Stormbank Thunderbirds off you.",
        'The thunderbirds are drawn to anyone carrying a mote. Carry them low and fast.'),
    'scq_the_hollow_storm': (
        "There's a storm in the middle of the Stormbank, south-west of Lenswatch, with an eye in the middle of it, and every bolt in the bank goes into that eye. I'm calling it the Hollow Storm, because that's all I can see of it. If it keeps pulling the lightning in, sooner or later it'll let it all go at once. Lenswatch is close enough to feel it. Put it out before it does.",
        "Go in when the bank's quiet. It only throws lightning when it's full."),
    'scq_guns_on_the_chainhold': (
        "Twice now they've fired on my ship from the Chainhold, north-west of Lenswatch, and the second time they took a strip off her hull. She's the oldest ship in the House's fleet, and she's our only way home. I've patched her twice and I won't have the wood for a third time. I'd rather lose my rank than lose her. Cross the chains onto the islet, and silence the Ascendancy Artillerists and Ascendancy Bombardiers working the guns.",
        "Spike the guns if you've time. A gun with no crew can find a new one."),
    'scq_wolves_on_the_cloud': (
        "My porters carry the ship's stores across the cloud from the Survey Dock, and every Cloudrunner Wolf on the shelf has learned to follow them. The Shelf Stalkers are worse, because you can't see them in the mist until they're on you. I lost a porter's leg to one last week. The shelf is west of Lenswatch, across the gangway. Thin them out so my porters can work without a guard on every one.",
        "The stalkers hunt the porters' route. Walk it slowly, carrying something."),
    'scq_ask_them_yourself': (
        "I've asked Warden Varn twice if we're free to go, and twice he's told me it's complicated. He's kind about it, and that's the worst part. We moved off the cloud into Lenswatch last week, onto our own rock, and nobody asked us about that either. Take him this letter. You're not one of his guests, so maybe he'll give you a straight answer.",
        "He's usually by the court in the evenings. He likes to watch the lens."),
    'scq_the_two_they_took': (
        "The soldiers took two of ours when they hit the stones, Lise and Tomasz. I found out they're being kept in the hangar on the Chainhold, the islet north-west of Lenswatch, and the Construct Hounds guard it. Lise taught me to cook up here, and Tomasz still owes me money. They've been in there nine days now. Get through the hounds and get into that hangar.",
        "They'll follow you out if they see a face that isn't Aetherian."),
    'scq_two_kinds_of_guest': (
        "Ilaren Vey is the only one of them who comes to the Annex without a notebook, and he eats what Beatriz cooks. I still don't trust him, because I've never trusted any of them. But he stood on the stones when the soldiers came, and he's still here. He's in the court, up the plank from our rock. Take him this bread, from the Annex.",
        "Tell him Beatriz made it. He'll eat it faster."),
    'scq_sky_medicine': (
        "I ran out of real medicine in my first year up here, so now I make it. The trolls showed me a herb that grows on the crown, khadgar's whisker, that brings down a fever better than anything I had in Beirut. I've got three fevers on our rock this week. It grows on the crown, west of Lenswatch across the gangway. Gather some for me, please, and I'll show you what I make of it.",
        "Take the leaves with the purple edges. The green ones haven't come into their strength."),
    'scq_gold_dust_salve': (
        "The Gilded Moths in the Goldenwood, west of Lenswatch on the crown's north arm, shed a dust that numbs whatever it touches. I've tried it on a burn, and it works. Bring me Pinches of Gold Dust and I'll make a salve. There'll be enough for the Annex and for the trolls at Spearhold. They're bleeding as much as we are.",
        'Shake the moths gently into a jar. If you swat them, the dust goes everywhere.'),
    'scq_hound_gyros': (
        "The Construct Hounds on the Chainhold, north-west of Lenswatch, run on cloud, on chains, on anything, and they don't ever fall over. Something in their chests keeps them upright. I designed bridges in Brno, and balance is the whole job. Bring me those Hound Gyros. If I can understand how they balance a dog, I might understand how they balance an island.",
        "The gyro's still spinning when it comes out. Don't drop it, it'll roll off the edge."),
    'scq_how_to_anchor_an_island': (
        "Lenswatch is an island that floats, and it's held still by one anchor and a chain. Now that I understand the gyros, I need to see it. I've asked to see it three times, and three times they've said later. The gravity anchor is on the east side of the island, by the mooring. You're a guest of the House, so walk over to it, look at it properly, and come back and tell me everything you saw.",
        "Count the links in the chain. I'll know a lot from that number alone."),
    'scq_every_islet': (
        "I climbed this tree from the roots so I could be first to the top, and I wasn't. So now I'm going to stand on everything up here that anyone's ever named. The Driftlets are chained off the south side of the cloud, south-west of Lenswatch, and the two at the far end of the chains are the ones nobody's walked. I'd go myself, but my ankle hasn't forgiven me for the tree. Walk them for me.",
        "Stamp on each one so it knows somebody's been there. I always do."),
    'scq_lend_him_the_lens': (
        "De village I was born in is down dere in Stranglethorn, and from here it's only a smudge. I come to de Lookdown every mornin' to make sure it's still dere. Dey say de sky people's lens can see a coin on de ground. Take dis charm to whoever keeps de lens in Lenswatch, over de gangway on de east edge of de cloud. Ask him to look for my village.",
        "De charm's carved wit' de river bend we live on. He'll know where to look."),
    'scq_keep_it_shut': (
        "Every word I can read on the Sunken Seal means keep it shut. I've brought my rubbings in here to the Lens Hall, but the ring itself is out on the cloud, west of Lenswatch. The Waking Guardians were set there to keep it shut, and they've woken up wrong, the way a sleeper wakes up fighting. The Unbound Storms were chained in the stones, and now they're coming loose. Put them both down before the ring shakes itself apart.",
        'The storms orbit the guardians. Take a guardian down and its storm wanders off.'),
    'scq_the_stone_that_woke': (
        "The biggest of the ring's wardens has stood up off its plinth at the Sunken Seal, west of Lenswatch out on the cloud. The Kharad cut its name into its chest, and I think it means the stone that keeps watch. It's not keeping watch now. It's tearing at the seal it was made to guard. Stop it before it opens the thing for us.",
        'Read the name on its chest before you strike. It deserves that much.'),
}
